I added one figure to the post. It sits right after the "utilitarian migration" paragraph, the passage the whole post builds on: owners aren't scrolling, they're solving problems. It builds without type errors, shows no console errors, and doesn't scroll sideways at 375px. I looked at it on a phone-width screen both mid-animation and when finished.

**What it shows:** small figures in the site's accent colour walk away from a phone labelled "the feed / passive scrolling". Footprints lead to four market stalls, one for each problem the passage lists: find workers, vet tools, unfiltered advice, automate tasks. One faded figure stays by the phone, labelled "some still scrolling". I added that because the text says owners "are moving toward" these places, not that all of them have gone.

**One thing to check:** the post gives no split between the four stalls, so each stall gets one owner. The caption says the even split is illustrative.

**Animation:** the walk plays once, about 3 seconds, when the figure scrolls into view. Before that, and for anyone with reduced motion turned on, it shows the finished scene.

